<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_66f14f762d9ed93be7e45532f52e341584cfa69a96a4b48ae6ab5277a1a358e7_n0055/e_0018> <http://digistrucmed.org/spanConfidence> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_66f14f762d9ed93be7e45532f52e341584cfa69a96a4b48ae6ab5277a1a358e7_n0055/tu_0009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "To avoid large volumes of fluid intake. A fluid restriction of 1.5–2 L/day may be considered in patients with severe HF/hyponatraemia to relieve symptoms and congestion. To avoid dehydration: where fluids are restricted, increase intake during periods of high heat/humidity and/or nausea/vomiting." .
